// =============================================================================================
// Interfaces.fusion - Fusion's own (built-in) interfaces (Task 32.5, 2026-10-31)
// =============================================================================================
//
// The interfaces Fusion itself provides. Like Fusion_showcase.fusion it does NOT compile: a
// built-in interface can't be declared again, so each is shown as a comment, then a class
// using it. Working examples: SYNTAX_REFERENCE.md (syntax_interfaces, syntax_to_string,
// syntax_object_copies, syntax_default).
//
//   [built]     works in the compiler today
//   [designed]  decided, not built yet - the task number says which task builds it
//
// A built-in interface is added to a program only when one of its classes implements it, and
// its name can't be used for an interface of your own ("'ToString' is Fusion's own interface").
//
// Fusion's own interfaces
//   ToString        [built 32.5b]     how an object prints
//   Cloneable       [built 32.5b]     a class that makes its own copy
//   Default         [built 32.5b]     a variable of the type is never null
//   Collection<T>   [designed 32.4]   anything foreach can loop over
//   List<T>         [designed 32.6]   List as an interface, with a default implementation
//   Service<T>      [designed 42.21]  every kind of service (BasicService, HotPathService, ...)
//
// Not built in: Shape, Named and the like in the tests and examples are a program's own


// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// [built 32.5b] ToString - how an object prints
//     interface ToString { string function toString() }
// print, format, "{x}" and toString(x) use it - also through an interface value. Without it
// an object prints its class name, and the compiler warns once per class.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
class Car implements ToString {
    string name
    constructor(string name) { this.name = name }
    string function toString() : "Car " + name
}


// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// [built 32.5b] Cloneable - a class that makes its own copy
//     interface Cloneable { <the class> function clone() }
// byVal calls its clone(). Needed only when a field is nocopy (a connection, a lock); any
// other object is copied by byVal without it - a new object, each field copied byVal (D.088).
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
class Account implements Cloneable {
    nocopy Database db                  // [built 32.5b] set only in a constructor or clone()
    noshare List<string> history        // [built 32.5b] handed out only as a copy (byVal)
    public int balance
    constructor() { db = Database() }
    Account function clone() {
        Account copy = Account()        // a new connection, not a shared one
        copy.balance = balance
        return copy
    }
}


// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// [built 32.5b] Default - a variable of the type is never null
//     interface Default { constructor() }      // a constructor without arguments
// The compiler makes the object when a variable, field or static is declared; `= null` lets
// the old object go and makes a new default one. The constructor may be private.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
class Settings implements Default {
    public int size = 3
    private constructor() { size = 5 }
}


// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// [designed 32.4] Collection<T> - anything foreach can loop over (Decisions.md D.085)
//     interface Collection<T> {
//         bool function add(T item)                      // true when it was added
//         bool function remove(T item)                   // removes one; true when one was there
//         int function length()                          // len as quick typing
//         bool function isEmpty()
//         bool function contains(T item)
//         bool function addAll(Collection<T> items)
//         bool function removeAll(Collection<T> items)
//         bool function keepOnly(Collection<T> items)    // retainAll as quick typing
//         void function clear()
//     }
// Arrays, Lists and Maps implement it, and so can a class of your own. A looped collection
// isn't changed inside the loop - your own only with [collections] allowChangeWhileLooping.
// Still to decide: how foreach walks your own one (an iterator?); what arrays and Maps give.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
class Team implements Collection<Person> {
    List<Person> people
    // ... each function of Collection<Person>, mostly passed on to `people`
}


// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// [designed 32.6] List<T> - an interface with a default implementation
// `List<string> names` is never null: it gets the default implementation, which can be
// swapped for another (program to an interface, not an implementation).
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------


// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// [designed 42.21] Service<T> - every kind of service (files/Service.md)
//     interface Service<T> {
//         void function send(T request)      // a caller puts a request in the mailbox
//         T function fetch()                 // the worker fetches its next request
//         void function start()
//         void function stop()
//         ServiceState function state()
//         int function waiting()             // requests in the mailbox
//     }
// Implemented by BasicService (one worker thread), SharedService (a temporary one, made by
// the compiler), FileService, DatabaseService and HotPathService (`hotpath service`).
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------


// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// [built 32.5a] An interface of your own - for comparison (not built in)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
interface Shape {
    float function area()
}

class Circle implements Shape, ToString {
    float r
    constructor(float r) { this.r = r }
    float function area() : 3.14159 * r * r
    string function toString() : "a circle"
}

void function main() {
    Shape s = Circle(2.0)               // [built 32.5a] the object's own area() runs
    print("{s}")                        // [built 32.5b] its toString(): a circle
    Settings settings                   // [built 32.5b] Default: made here, never null
    Account copy = byVal Account()      // [built 32.5b] Cloneable: its clone() makes it
}
